QuestGuidance.Register("en",138,{
[4385]="700300F9\n1\tBring Cíllan's first payment to Frithbéorth\tFrithbéorth is in Harwick, waiting patiently for a delivery of three-hundred gold to secure the purchase of his family's large manor. You should bring Cíllan's down payment to Frithbéorth and see if he will accept it.\n2\tSpeak to Frithbéorth to enter the manor\tFrithbéorth reluctantly hands over the keys to his family's large manor.\n3\tReturn to Cíllan at the refugee camp\tCíllan awaits you at the refugees' camp outside of Harwick. You should hasten to Cíllan to hand her the keys and tell her of the deal with Frithbéorth... and it would be wise to mention the rats as well.\n",
[4386]="70018F7D\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Nanduhirion (total: 10)\tOrcs can be found all along the road that leads through Nanduhirion, the Dimrill Dale, north-west of Talan Haldir. Hadroneth has asked you to thin the numbers of the Orcs that have come forth from within the mountains.\n2\tTalk to Hadroneth\tHadroneth is on Talan Haldir, along the banks of Nimrodel. The Elf Hadroneth is waiting for you to report of your success slaying the Orcs that have poured from the Gates of Moria into Nanduhirion.\n",
[4387]="7000B961\n1\tTalk to Ringhul\030Bring the brooch to Ringhul on the High Moor\tRinghul is at his post on the High Moor, north and east of Tâl Bruinen. Candelleth told you that the brooch you found belong to a former scout of hers named Ringhul, who is now posted upon the High Moor, and suggested that you bring it to him and inquire about the giant.\n2\tTalk to Arifael\tArifael lives on the slope of Amon Nendir, south of the High Moor on the eastern edge of the Trollshaws. Elrohir is concerned about the giant footprints you saw in Tâl Bruinen and wants you to ask Arifael if he has heard of giants wandering that far south.\n",
[4388]="7001B225\n1\tTalk to Andreg at the Greenway Fort\tAndreg is at the Old Greenway Fort, west of Hengstacer. Oddvarr has asked you to tell the Ranger Andreg that he is grateful for the Rangers' assistance and that Orcs have come down from the eastern stretches of the North Downs as well.\n",
[4389]="7003FDE5\n1\tDefeat corsair captains on their ships (total: 3)\tWhile the captains live, the corsairs can retreat or reinforce.\n",
[4390]="7000C766\n1\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin is encamped outside the entrance to Goblin-town. Nogmeldir has asked you to find Glóin and ask for aid finding Glorwen.\n2\tTalk to Glorwen\tGlorwen is imprisoned in Goblin-town. Nogmeldir has asked you to find and rescue the scout Glorwen.\n",
[4391]="7001ABE6\n1\tDefeat brigands at the Old Sweetgrass Farm (total: 12)\tMake your way to the Old Sweetgrass Farm north-east of Adso's Camp and help Adso drive the brigands away from his camp. Adso can think of no way to drive the brigands off that does not involve violence. He sent you to fight and defeat brigands near Old Sweetgrass Farm.\n2\tTalk to Adso Haybank\tAdso Haybank awaits your return at his camp to the south-west of Old Sweetgrass Farm along the Great East Road. You should return to Adso Haybank with news of your success.\n",
[4392]="7001520A\n1\tKill dragonets in the Old Silvertine City (total: 10)\tDiseased dragonets can be found in the Old Silvertine City in the southern Silvertine Lodes. You should slay many of the diseased dragonets.\n2\tInform Öndótt that the dragonet population has been lessened\tÖndótt stands at the top of the stairwell in the Old Silvertine City. You should return to Öndótt.\n",
[4393]="70027E8F\n1\tCollect symbols of the White Hand (total: 12)\tDragon-clansmen in the White Hand encampment show signs of belonging to Isengard instead of acting upon their own motives. You should collect evidence of the White Hand from the Dragon-clan warriors of the encampment.\n2\tReturn to Guto at his encampment\tGuto can be found at his small camp-site in the southern fields of Trum Dreng. You should return to Guto with the White Hand symbols you collected.\n",
[4394]="70055003\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Draigoch's Lair -- Discovery\n",
[4395]="7005AB19\n1\tDefeat drakes and worms in Flogalith (total: 15)\tDrakes and worms nest high in the cliffs above the Welkin-lofts. Their presence endangers your mission here. You should defeat drakes and worms in Flogalith.\n2\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tYou have defeated many worm-kind in Flogalith. You should talk to Molkha.\n",
[4396]="700494CC\n1\tDefeat fire drakes (total: 12)\tFire drakes can be found in Talath Úrui, mainly near the Ghâshghurm. You should defeat any fire drakes and their offspring that you encounter.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many fire drakes in Talath Úrui.\n",
[4397]="7005B1F1\n1\tDestroy drake eggs at Kordh Gúrat\tDestroying the drake eggs at Kordh Gúrat would keep the drakelings from becoming a threat.\n2\tDestroying the drake eggs at Kordh Gúrat would keep the drakelings from becoming a threat.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many of the drake eggs at Kordh Gúrat.\n",
[4398]="70069447\n1\tCraft a crate of potions for the Umbar Scholar's Guild\tThe recipe needed to complete this quest is available for purchase. Purchase the quest recipe from the guild leader. Pack a crate of potions for Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver a crate of potions to the Umbar Scholar's Guild Leader\tProvide the crate of potions to the Umbar Scholar's Guild Leader.\n",
[4399]="7006B10B\n1\tCraft a crate of potions for the Umbar Scholar's Guild\tThe recipe needed to complete this quest is available for purchase. Purchase the quest recipe from the guild leader. Pack a crate of potions for Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver a crate of potions to the Umbar Scholar's Guild Leader\tProvide the crate of potions to the Umbar Scholar's Guild Leader.\n",
[4400]="7006944F\n1\tComplete Umbar Scholar's Guild daily orders (total: 5)\tComplete requests from the Umbar Scholar's Guild. You can acquire these quests from the Umbar Scholar's Guild Leader in the Umbar Baharbêl craft guild hall.\n2\tCompleted\tYou completed many Umbar scholar requests.\n",
[4401]="7004DCE2\n1\tCollect 'healing draughts' for ailing Stout-axes (total: 8)\t'Healing draughts' can be found on feasting tables in the Hall Under the Mountain. Náth hopes to help the remaining ailing Stout-axes by giving them 'healing draughts'.\n2\tAiling Stout-axes can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have gathered 'healing draughts' for the ailing Stout-axes and should now deliver them.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have aided the ailing Stout-axes.\n",
[4402]="7005AB0D\n1\tDefeat wolves in Draurákh (total: 14)\030Defeat Snárfrek\tNáth has asked you to find the wolf den called Draurákh west of Fellgát and defeat the wolves within. You should defeat wolves in Draurákh, including the pack leader, Snárfrek.\n2\tTalk to Náth at Fellgát\tYou have cleared the wolf pack from Draurákh. You should talk to Náth in Fellgát.\n",
[4403]="7006605F\n1\tTalk to the lumber camp labourer\030Talk to the tax collector\030Talk to Stable-hand\tDervorin would like you to see if anyone in Ethring has any information regarding Dravron. Talk to the citizens of Ethring.\n2\tTalk to Dervorin\tYou have asked around about Dravron and should report back to Dervorin with your findings. Talk to Dervorin in Ethring.\n",
[4404]="7006576F\n1\tFind a good place to hide the false map\tAerin has asked you to hide a false map somewhere in Hata Kebir, east of Aerthir. Find a place to hide the map.\n2\tTalk to Aerin\tYou have successfully hidden the map, and should inform Aerin. Talk to Aerin in Aerthir.\n",
[4405]="70015E13\n1\tThe site for the false camp is south-west of Limlaer, between Porth Cadlus and Goeolhad, in a boulder-encircled basin. Limlaer has tasked you with setting a trap for the scouts of the Enemy.\t\n2\tTalk to Limlaer\tLimlaer is south-east of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road. You should return to Limlaer with news of your success.\n",
[4406]="7000004E\n1\tSummon and defeat Shadepaw\tThe stone table where you should pour Mugwort's gruel is at the end of a southward path near a signpost on the road through Nain Enidh. Old Mugwort asked you to take the special gruel he prepared to an ancient stone near the lair of the Wargs. The stench of it should draw forth their leader.\n2\tTalk to Old Mugwort\tOld Mugwort is at the camp on the east side of Minas Eriol. After drawing Shadepaw's pack into the open, you defeated the Warg-leader. Old Mugwort will want to hear of your victory.\n",
[4407]="7004A8E7\n1\tDefeat ravening carrion-flies in Rath Cail (total: 8)\tRavening carrion-flies can be found in Rath Cail. You have been beset by ravening carrion-flies in Rath Cail and should defeat them to make clear the way deeper into Lhingris.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many ravening carrion-flies in Rath Cail.\n",
[4408]="70043099\n1\tTalk to Faltharan, Son of Sirgon\tFaltharan can be found overlooking the eastern gate of Pelargir. Angbor has grown concerned by the behaviour of Faltharan, the son of the Lord of Pelargir, and wishes for you to speak to him.\n2\tCalm Faltharan and ask of his troubles\tFaltharan can be found overlooking the eastern gate of Pelargir. You have found Faltharan and should now try to calm him before he rushes out into combat.\n3\tTalk to Faltharan\tFaltharan can be found overlooking the eastern gate of Pelargir. You have listened to Faltharan's troubles, and should now assure him of your intent to help him.\n",
[4409]="70047BE5\n1\tPoke the Ranger and attempt to wake him from the trance\tThe remaining Rangers can be found somewhere in the southern reaches of the Dead Marshes in northern Dagorlad. Faramir has informed you that the rest of the Rangers fled northward into the dangerous shallows of the Dead Marshes. You should seek them out at once.\n2\tTalk to Faramir at the foot of Dol Acharn\tFaramir can be found at the foot of Dol Acharn in Dagorlad. You have freed the remaining Rangers from their trances and sent them back to Haerondir. You should now speak to Faramir near Dol Acharn.\n",
[4410]="70015207\n1\tCollect fungus-spores from Globsnaga Orcs (total: 6)\tGlobsnaga Orcs can be found on the banks near The Chamber of Dark Waters, south of the Rotting Cellar. Gyrgir wants you to gather fungus-spores from several Globsnaga Orcs. He believes with them, he will be able to learn things important for creating an antidote.\n2\tReturn to Gyrgir with the spores\030Collect Fungal Spore (total: 6)\tGyrgir is in Hulwul-nefekh, west of The Chamber of Dark Waters. You defeated several Globsnaga Orcs and managed to gather enough fungus-spores for the dwarves to research. You should return to Gyrgir in Hulwul-nefekh and deliver the spores.\n",
[4411]="7003E40D\n1\tDefeat wood-flies in Fangorn Forest (total: 12)\tWood-flies can be found throughout Fangorn Forest to the west of Derndingle. The Huorn seeks your aid in thinning the number of wood-flies in Fangorn Forest. You should defeat them.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam's Huorn\tYou have slain many wood-flies and reduced the threat they posed to the Entwash and nearby trees.\n",
[4412]="70066CBF\n1\tCollect turtle shells (total: 8)\tMaelvír has asked you to bring back shells from the dread-turtles inhabiting a nearby island. You can hunt dread-turtles on the island of Loeg Thangalf, in Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tReturn to Maelvír\tWith multiple dread-turtle shells in hand, you should return to Maelvír. Maelvír is at Mereham, in central Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[4413]="7000D3CE\n1\tThree lesser watching-stones can be found somewhere within the city of Dûn Covád, far to the north of Aughaire, in the western hills of Fasach-falroid. Sorkha wants you to find the locations of three lesser watching-stones within Dûn Covád.\t\n2\tTalk to Sorkha\tSorkha is in the Búth Luikh in Aughaire. You have located three lesser watching-stones within the city of Dûn Covád and should return now to Sorkha with the knowledge of their locations.\n",
[4414]="7002EF21\n1\tThornhope lies just down the road from Béortnoth's camp. Thane Béortnoth has asked you to search Thornhope for other survivors.\t\n2\tTalk to Béortnoth outside of Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is encamped outside of Thornhope. You should return to Béortnoth with news of your findings.\n",
[4415]="700442BB\n1\tComplete Quest: A Path for Aragorn: Orcs\030Complete Quest: A Path for Aragorn: Captains\030Complete Quest: A Path for Aragorn: Siege\030Complete Quest: A Path for Aragorn: Trolls\030Complete Quest: A Path for Aragorn: Tents\tTurgon can be found at the southern gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Turgon and assist him with clearing the port of the Harlond.\n2\tSpeak with Turgon\tTurgon can be found at the southern gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Turgon.\n",
[4416]="70053151\n1\tRead 'Sharkey's Orders'\tSharkey's orders can be found in your inventory. You have discovered orders from Sharkey after defeating Sharkey's lieutenant at Sharkey's Slough.\n2\tInvestigate Tûn Melen\tTûn Melen can be found in the south-western reaches of the Gladden Fields. You have found orders from Sharkey detailing excavations at a place called Tûn Melen. According to the orders, it seems to be located to the south-west of Sharkey's Slough.\n3\tThe ruined excavation site at Tûn Melen can be found somewhere among the ruined dredging machines in the northern reaches of Tûn Melen. Sharkey's orders told of a ruined excavation site in the northern reaches of Tûn Melen. You should find it and explore it.\t\n4\tFind the warrens of Tûn Melen\tThe warrens of Tûn Melen can be found to the south of Tûn Melen in the south-western Gladden Fields. You have searched the ruined excavation site at Tûn Melen, but you found no sign of Sharkey or his men. You should continue your search to the south and find the warrens of Tûn Melen.\n5\tInvestigate the warrens of Tûn Melen\tThe warrens of Tûn Melen can be found to the south of Tûn Melen in the south-western Gladden Fields. You have found the warrens of Tûn Melen. You should investigate them, but proceed carefully, as Sharkey and his men are likely gathered inside.\n6\tTalk to the imprisoned Woodman in the warrens of Tûn Melen\tThe imprisoned Woodman can be found in a small alcove to the right of the entrance to the warrens of Tûn Melen. After entering the warrens of Tûn Melen, you heard a faint cry from a Woodman in a cage. You should speak to the imprisoned Woodman and learn what has happened in the warrens of Tûn Melen.\n",
})
